---
import LibraryLayout from "../../layouts/LibraryLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/section-pages.css";
---
<LibraryLayout activeSection="privacy" title="Privacy Notice — Ridwanah" description="Understand what information the current Ridwanah website collects and how third-party resources are handled.">
  <div id="top" class="policy-page">
    <div class="library-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy notice</span></div>
    <section class="policy-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> PRIVACY BY DESIGN</div>
      <h1>Your privacy<br /><em>deserves care.</em></h1>
      <p>This notice describes the current Ridwanah website as built. It should be reviewed and updated before any accounts, forms, analytics, advertising or other data-collection features are introduced.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="policy-content">
      <section><h2>What the current website asks for</h2><p>The current static website does not ask visitors to create an account, submit a medical history or enter personal health information through a form. Search and category filters run in the visitor’s browser to filter content already displayed on the page.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Information handled by hosting services</h2><p>When a website is accessed, the hosting and network services used to deliver it may process technical request information such as IP address, browser details and request logs. The exact information, retention period and legal basis will depend on the hosting provider and its settings. These details must be confirmed when production hosting is selected.</p></section>
      <section><h2>External links and video embeds</h2><p>Ridwanah links to external organisations and embeds selected videos using YouTube’s privacy-enhanced player domain. When a visitor opens an external site or plays an embedded video, the external provider may process technical information under its own policies. Review the provider’s privacy information before using those services.</p><p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.youtube.com/howyoutubeworks/our-commitments/protecting-user-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube information about user data ↗</a></p></section>
      <section><h2>Health information</h2><p>Do not send confidential medical details, identity documents or other sensitive information through public comments, social media or general project channels. The current website is not designed to receive, store or assess personal health information.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Cookies and analytics</h2><p>No first-party analytics or advertising tools are intentionally included in the current website code. Third-party embedded media and future hosting services may operate differently. Any analytics, advertising, account or tracking feature added later must be assessed and disclosed before release.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Children and young people</h2><p>Ridwanah aims to make health education accessible to a broad audience. The current site does not provide user accounts or request personal details from children. Parents, caregivers and educators should guide young people when using external media and health resources.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Changes to this notice</h2><p>This notice must be updated when the site’s hosting, data flows or features change. A final production privacy notice should identify the responsible legal entity or contact, applicable retention practices and a monitored privacy contact route before launch.</p></section>
      <p class="policy-last-updated">Project privacy notice — drafted 20 November 2026. Review before public launch.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</LibraryLayout>
